  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Siemens 840D and Doosan DNM mill posts always wrote millimetre numbers but no unit word, so a control left in inch by power-on or the last program read every coordinate 25.4x too long. Each now states the unit it writes, before any motion:\n\n- `fanuc.cps`, `haas.cps`, `mazak.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps`: `G21` in a block of its own at the end of `onOpen` (after `%`, the O word / name and any inverted-axis notes).\n- `sinumerik.cps`: `G710` (metric lengths **and** feeds; `G71` would leave F in the basic system's unit) inside each section's opening block (`N.. G17 G710 G90 G54 G40 G80`), so the N numbering of every existing program is unchanged.\n\nScope follows the maintainer's scope change on #901: unit word only. The posts do not read `machine.units` and refuse nothing; where the program's unit is chosen (document-level setting) and inch output are #902. Decision record: `docs/decisions/901-post-unit-word.md`.\n\nTest-side follow-ons: the `macro_b` probe reader models `G21` (mm, its unit; G20 stays unmodelled); `regression_models` posted-line counts +1.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning tests (new suite `post_unit_word`, one per post): `fanuc_states_g21_before_any_motion`, `haas_states_g21_before_any_motion`, `mazak_states_g21_before_any_motion`, `sinumerik_states_g710_before_any_motion`, `doosan_dnm_states_g21_before_any_motion` - the word precedes the first motion line on no machine, a metric and an inch machine file (both the mounted and the raw-file door), and no inch word is written.\n- Goldens regenerated only for these posts (91 files under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/`); the diff is exactly 76 added `G21` lines and 18 Sinumerik preamble lines gaining `G710` - nothing else moved.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick`) green on the pre-merge head: all camcraft-app suites (the shared `macro_b` change selects them all), 947 s.\n- After `git merge origin/main` (#803 changed fanuc/doosan-dnm, merged cleanly): `cargo test -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --no-fail-fast` - 279 test binaries ok. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- camcraft-ui suites (no UI code changed; the G-code viewer reads the program dynamically) and the release-lane `--ignored` heavy lanes.\n- An 840D program with no section at all carries no G710 (only the end lift); not reachable from a real posting - noted in the decisions file.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM posts write G21 and the Siemens 840D post writes G710 before any motion, so a control left in inch never reads the mm program as inches (#901)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #901\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
